A plain function with a variadic parameter that nothing produces: []Option is unprovided,
so it becomes an injector input, and the call spreads the parameter local with the ...
form (Serve(opts...)). Distinct from the produced-slice and interface-method variadic
fixtures.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Option struct{}
type Server struct{}

//plumb:build
func Serve(opts ...Option) *Server { return &Server{} }

//plumb:build
func Use(s *Server) int { return 0 }
